  "answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative launched on June 15th with Sarah Tan as the lead. The initial budget was $500,000 for Phase One, which was later adjusted to $550,000 to cover real-time analytics integration. The executive board subsequently approved a total budget of $2 million covering all phases. Key milestones include the completion of the testing phase (celebrated on October 10th) and a breakthrough in predictive analytics reported in Phase Two. The team has expanded with Mike Chen and Lisa Ray, and a compliance plan budget of $55,000 has been approved. Partnership discussions with TechInnovate are underway, and a detailed progress report is scheduled for the November 20th staff meeting."
